{
  "$comment": "Controlling powers for globe colours. Upstream spells the same power several ways across years (UK, Great Britain, United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland…) and sometimes misspells it; `aliases` maps every spelling to one canonical `power`, which picks the colour, so an empire keeps one colour from snapshot to snapshot. The displayed 'Controlled by' text keeps the period spelling. Where upstream records a colony as ruling itself, build-snapshots.mjs takes the ruler from rulers.json (dated), or else infers it only from a name of the form 'Region (Power)' with a power listed here, or from a leading adjective in `adjectives` ('Dutch Guiana'); every inference is printed so it can be reviewed. Add an entry to rulers.json, or an explicit {name, subjecto} entry to name-overrides.json, when that rule is wrong.",
